  "solution": {
    "text": "Since only one letters can not be in wrong envelope so that at least two letters are in wrong envelope means all the letters are not in right envelopes.<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>720</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>719</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo></math> number of ways, so that all the letters are in wrong envelops</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>265</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>719</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>265</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>454</mn></math></p>",
